# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. GitHub Pages is only free on public repos, so everything
# committed here is world-readable and Google-indexable. Read that sentence
# again before adding an exception to any rule below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The acronym glossary is IBM sales/licensing terminology and must never be
# committed. It arrives at runtime, base64-decoded from the ACRONYMS_JSON
# GitHub Actions secret, and is deleted when the job ends. Wildcards are
# deliberate — a rotated copy left behind as acronyms.json.bak would otherwise
# be swept up by `git add -A`.
acronyms.json*

# Everything derived from the glossary: the daily term lessons and the
# curator's cross-links, which quote definitions verbatim. These render into
# the email only. data/briefs/ holds the public half and IS committed.
data/private/

# Per-run scratch handed between stages. Regenerated every run.
data/run/

# Extra email recipients. Addresses are personal data and this repo is
# public; the list is loaded at runtime from the RECIPIENTS_JSON secret.
recipients.json*

# Credentials — supplied from Actions secrets, same pattern as bwr-pipeline.
.env*
gmail_credentials.json*
gmail_token.json*
client_secret_*.json
*.pem

# Python
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# macOS
.DS_Store
